      "tree_id": "5c6266f4b6f1ed3c7d0e46b8f900748328527001",
      "message": "Open Catalan for direct submissions (issue route, split build)\n\nThe split-build smoke passed on 2026-10-27: run 40497685416, test issue #68, Sean Litsey's\nexponent-1091 proof in the Submission layout (fixture verifier-smoke-catalan@a3d4849). Job 1 built\nin 6178 s (peak 9.79 GB, no swap) and packed 23,792 files (2.94 GB, 0 skipped). In job 2, the Lean\nkernel (8250 s) and the axiom audit (only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound) ended 142 minutes\nafter prepare, so 178 minutes of the 320-minute deadline were left. lean_path had the dependency\npackages, then the root build folder, then the toolchain.\n\n- CLOSED is now {'subset-sum'}. The issue form offers catalan.\n- The scan skips an issue with the label test, as the acknowledgement pass does. Before, a closed\n  Catalan kept the smoke issue out of the scan; now only the dispatch runs a test issue.\n- README, docs/targets.md and docs/execution.md give the target, the range (0 <= mu <= 100000000,\n  smaller is better, issue route only) and the split-run limits: only the final result posts,\n  the queue is held for the whole run (up to about 12 hours), nanoda usually ends incomplete.\n- New docs/convert-layout.md: how to move a proof repository (Litsey's as the example) into the\n  Submission layout, with the general form of the script that made the fixture. Checked: on\n  Litsey 50672b8 it writes the 2620 fixture files byte for byte (plus the unused top-level\n  CatalanMeasure.lean).\n- Tests: Catalan is open and selected as a split run against the row gate; a test issue is not\n  scanned.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
